--- !u!114 &686385069
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 686385067}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 23287d684813c8549b9f1a773541174a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OnboardingController
  introPanel: {fileID: 1445313521}
  tooltipPanel: {fileID: 1826359149}
  tooltipText: {fileID: 590785178}
  introStartButton: {fileID: 2051123434}
  tooltipNextButton: {fileID: 646282155}
  introTitle: Welcome to NovaCorp!
  introBody: You've just been hired as System Architect. Your job is to build and
    protect the company's digital infrastructure. Keep the network running, the revenue
    flowing, and the attackers out. Good luck.
  introTitleText: {fileID: 1001737888}
  introBodyText: {fileID: 1986996439}
  screens:
  - text: You are the new system architect. Everything you need to build the company's
      network is right here in the toolbar. Once the game starts, click and drag
      a node onto any tile on the grid to place it.
    arrows:
    - {fileID: 1813694744}
  - text: This is a Service node. It is the customer-facing part of the network and
      the thing that generates revenue for NovaCorp. On its own it does nothing.
      It needs infrastructure behind it to function.
    arrows:
    - {fileID: 1559272951}
  - text: A Service needs a Server to process its requests, and that Server needs
      a Database to store its data. Connect the three and you have a working revenue
      chain. Leave any link missing and the money stops flowing.
    arrows:
    - {fileID: 1799027357}
    - {fileID: 216845421}
  - text: This is a Firewall. It does not generate revenue, but it protects the nodes
      connected to it from attacks. The more nodes it covers, the harder it works.
      Spread your firewalls out rather than relying on just one.
    arrows:
    - {fileID: 494253540}
  - text: This is your workspace. Click and drag nodes from the toolbar onto the
      tiles to start building. Each tile can hold one node.
    arrows:
    - {fileID: 960616330}
  - text: See the small dots on the edges of each placed node? Click one of those
      dots and drag to a dot on another placed node to connect them. That is how
      you build the chains that keep the network running.
    arrows:
    - {fileID: 1975672427}
    - {fileID: 1129990725}
  - text: When you place a node, you will be asked about its password. Generating
      a unique one costs $50 but keeps it isolated. Reusing the last password is
      free, but if one node gets compromised, every node sharing that password slowly
      goes down with it.
    arrows: []
  - text: You will be getting emails throughout the day. Reply to legitimate requests
      from coworkers. Some emails will be phishing attempts disguised as real messages,
      flag those. Reply to a phishing email and your reputation takes a hit. Ignoring
      emails does not help either, missed messages count against you.
    arrows:
    - {fileID: 1342008755}
  - text: Click any node you have placed to open its inspector. From here you can
      check its health, sell it for a partial refund, upgrade it, or rotate its password
      for $50 if you think it has been compromised.
    arrows: []
  - text: Keep an eye on these two bars. If your reputation hits zero, it is over.
      If your revenue stream stays broken for more than a minute, it is also over.
    arrows:
    - {fileID: 315347073}
    - {fileID: 1518176887}
  - text: That is everything. Fifteen minutes, one network, and a company counting
      on you. Good luck, Architect.
    arrows: []
  nextLabel: Got it
  startGameLabel: Start Game
